   "id": "lead-1",
   "section": "(lead)",
   "text": "Chandler v. Miller, 520 U.S. 305 (1997), was a case before the United States Supreme Court concerning the Constitutionality under the Fourth Amendment of a state statute requiring drug tests of all candidates for certain state offices.",
   "words": 38,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1",
    "Editor 3"
   ],
