  {
   "id": "sec2-1",
   "section": "Statute",
   "text": "In 1990, Georgia enacted a statute which required candidates for designated state office to certify that they had taken a drug test and obtained negative results.",
   "words": 26,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1",
    "Editor 5"
   ],
   "author_words": [
