  {
   "id": "sec6-2",
   "section": "Opinion of the Court",
   "text": "The Court noted that while the Fourth Amendment generally prohibits officials from conducting search and seizures without individualized suspicion, there does exist a \"closely guarded\" category of permissible suspicionless searches and seizures.",
